front:
Compute the sample variance of a long series of prices near 100,000 with small spread. Why does the naive formula \(\mathbb E[x^2]-\mathbb E[x]^2\) fail numerically, and what does Welford's update do? The naive code is:
<pre><code>double s = 0, s2 = 0;
for (double x : xs) { s += x; s2 += x*x; }
double var = s2/n - (s/n)*(s/n);</code></pre>
